{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790533535,"nonce":"KS9TesFn+xmVPX0nuVi2FZlvO6w=","message":"Implementation: a reloadable build plus a reload side module.\n\nBuild (library API in codegen::llvm_aot):\n- compile_modules_to_llvm_object_with(modules, bundle, target, entry, reloadable, output). When reloadable:\n  - AOT CHA is empty, so there are no direct calls, inlined trivial getters or inline constructors.\n  - #export members dispatch through wren_call_N rather than calling the body.\n  - The bootstrap registers each module's variable blob under its request_name and aliases (wlift_aot_register_module).\n- AotEntry::Reload compiles the last module of `modules` (the program's walk up to the changed module) as a PIC object. It defines wlift_reload_run(vm) -\u003e i32:\n  - wlift_aot_reload_begin(vm, name, new blob). It collects the old blob's non-core classes by name, points every registered name of the module at the new blob, and turns on class reuse.\n  - Constants, symbols, closures, runtime imports.\n  - Static imports copy from the running program's registered blobs (wlift_aot_import_module_var).\n  - Classes install onto the existing ObjClass (reset_class_for_reload, shared with the source reload).\n  - wlift_aot_reload_end: end reuse, flush the inline caches and the method cache.\n  - Then the module body runs.\n- link_wasm_reload(object, output) makes the side module, exporting wlift_reload_run.\n- reload_host_exports() returns the functions and data a reloadable program must export for later side modules: RUNTIME_FN_NAMES, AOT_ENTRY_NAMES and WASM_PROGRAM_LIBM as functions, wlift_error_pending as data. link_wasm_reloadable links a program with them.\n\nTest: tests/wasm_aot.rs a_reloaded_module_gives_its_classes_new_methods. It builds a reloadable library, runs it, and makes an instance. Then it compiles v2 of the module as a reload side module, loads it into the running instance with the dylink host, and calls wlift_reload_run. After that:\n- the old instance runs the new step;\n- the static export answers the new version;\n- a new import from another module resolves;\n- the body re-ran.\n\nBlockers 1-4 are handled as above. Still open:\n- Layout: a reload that adds fields leaves old instances too small (9ab7c22, same as the source reload).\n- A subclass in another module keeps its copies of methods inherited from a reloaded class. The source reload has the same limit.\n- Importers keep their copies of non-class variables. Closures made before the reload keep their old code.\n- Each reload leaves its old variable blob and constants rooted.\n- A reload object lowers the whole walk and relies on LLVM's DCE to drop the other modules, so compile time grows with the program.\n- No wlift CLI surface. Caribou calls the library API.","files":null}]}